# The root module: the file the engine runs (`cambra shop.cambra`). A root file's name starts with a
# lowercase letter, as every module path segment does.
#
# Result: 702. eu holds 101 + 251 - 10 = 342, and us holds 105 + 255 = 360.
#
# Run the root to test the program. `cambra check ledger.cambra` checks one module alone and prints
# its interface.

# `as` names the run; the name is the run's identity, its state included.
run ledger(fee=1) as eu
run ledger(fee=5) as us

for r in [10]:
    with begin():
        eu::refund(r)

# `await_final(x)` is the value of `x` once every block that may write it has finished. It is the
# only read of a final `Txn` value, it stands outside every block, and nothing names `x` after it.
await_final(eu::balance) + await_final(us::balance)
